<LegalPage
 title="Website Privacy | Align Therapy Group"
 description="Learn how the Align Therapy Group website handles information visitors may provide and basic technical website data."
 heading="Website Privacy"
 intro="This page explains privacy practices for the Align Therapy Group marketing website. It is not a Notice of Privacy Practices for counseling services."
>
 <section>
 <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>

 <p>
 You may choose to provide information when requesting an appointment or
 using a third-party service linked from this website. Please do not send
 diagnoses, medication information, trauma history, insurance identifiers,
 or other sensitive clinical details through ordinary website
 communication.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>Website analytics and technical information</h2>

 <p>
 The website and its hosting or network providers may process basic
 technical information needed to deliver and protect the site, such as an
 IP address, browser or device information, and the date and time of a
 request.
 </p>

 <p>
 Align Therapy Group also uses limited website analytics to understand
 general site use. The analytics script may record the page path being
 viewed, a general device category, the hostname of an external referring
 website, and interactions such as appointment, client portal, phone,
 email, or outbound-link clicks.
 </p>

 <p>
 The website analytics script is designed not to send URL query strings,
 form contents, clinical information, or a persistent visitor identifier.
 It uses a random temporary session identifier stored only in the
 browser’s session storage so general visits can be measured. The
 identifier rotates after inactivity or a limited period and is not
 designed to recognize a returning person across separate browser
 sessions. The analytics script does not use cookies or local storage.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>How information may be used</h2>

 <p>
 Website information may be used to operate and secure the site,
 understand general website use, improve performance and navigation, and
 understand which pages or links are useful to visitors.
 </p>

 <p>
 Information voluntarily provided through an appropriate contact or
 appointment system may be used to respond to a request, provide requested
 information, support practice administration, or direct someone to the
 appropriate secure system. Align Therapy Group does not use ordinary
 website communication to collect a clinical history.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>

 <p>
 This website may link to external services, including a
 practice-management system used for appointment requests or a client
 portal. Those services have their own privacy and security practices.
 Align Therapy Group is not responsible for the content or privacy
 practices of unrelated external websites.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>Website security</h2>

 <p>
 Reasonable care is used in operating this website, but no website or
 internet transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Avoid
 sending sensitive or urgent information through ordinary website
 channels.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>Changes to this page</h2>

 <p>
 This privacy page may be revised when website features, service
 providers, or practices change. The version published here is the
 current version.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>Privacy questions</h2>

 <p>
 Questions about this website privacy page may be directed to Align
 Therapy through the practice contact methods it publishes. Please do not
 include clinical or other sensitive personal information in an ordinary
 message.
 </p>
 </section>
</LegalPage>
